{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1395681-questions-on-the-nature-of-abysal-exaltation","id":1395681,"title":"Questions on the nature of Abysal Exaltation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-10T15:35:52-07:00","id":1395681,"title":"Questions on the nature of Abysal Exaltation","content":"This is probably somewhere in the older settings books, but I have little idea where to start looking...<br /> <br /> How long lasting is the Exaltation of an Abyssal? I know their soul is destined for Oblivion, but is the spark a one-and-done usage for the Deathlords?<br /> <br /> How much of their past lives do Abyssals typically remember? I've seen some stuff about the will of the Deathlords overriding things like personality to a degree, but not sure if that extends to the past lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T16:01:49-07:00","id":1395683,"title":"","content":"The Exaltation itself is just as enduring as a Solar spark or any other; in 1e/2e at least, the Abyssal Exaltation returns to a Monstrance of Celestial Portion. That's probably still the case.<br /> <br /> I don't remember anything about past lives being more or less a thing than for anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T16:45:55-07:00","id":1395690,"title":"","content":"Past lives are just memories. Not much you can do about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T17:33:24-07:00","id":1395705,"title":"","content":"Pretty much what's been said. In 2e abyssals were listed as theoretically immortal unless killed, though as they hadn't been around long enough that was more speculation than accurate, their soul would fall into Oblivion if they didn't get that one mirror charm that let them pretend to be Solars that stopped that, and the exaltation would go back to the Monstrance if it existed or go hunting for a new exalt if there wasn't a return place. Past life memories are more impressions and such that rubbed off on the exaltation, so those were still around seeing how it was mentioned that sunlight had a tendency to burn off past life memories from rogue abyssal exaltations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T21:08:14-07:00","id":1395757,"title":"","content":"I've never cared for the idea that Oblivion is the default fate of Abyssals. Existential issues aside, it seems like a dramatic waste to not have those Exalted have narratives of interacting with the ghosts of their past lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T22:21:49-07:00","id":1395763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1395681-questions-on-the-nature-of-abysal-exaltation?p=1395757#post1395757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never cared for the idea that Oblivion is the default fate of Abyssals. Existential issues aside, it seems like a dramatic waste to not have those Exalted have narratives of interacting with the ghosts of their past lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a bullet point in the whole removal of capital 'O' Oblivion. Though probably lower on the list than ensuring we didn't end up with more monsters or threats that &quot;can only be destroyed by being thrown into Oblivion&quot; or the ST coming up with their own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T03:38:26-07:00","id":1395803,"title":"","content":"The fact that you can't have ex-abyssal deathlords definitely needs to be rectified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T04:13:56-07:00","id":1395807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1395681-questions-on-the-nature-of-abysal-exaltation?p=1395757#post1395757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never cared for the idea that Oblivion is the default fate of Abyssals. Existential issues aside, it seems like a dramatic waste to not have those Exalted have narratives of interacting with the ghosts of their past lives.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I recall back in 1E there was a charm that guaranteed rising as a ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T04:35:42-07:00","id":1395809,"title":"","content":"Even in 2e, the roll to resist Oblivion was to roll the Abyssal's willpower at a difficulty of their essence. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T11:26:04-07:00","id":1395866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1395681-questions-on-the-nature-of-abysal-exaltation#post1395681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long lasting is the Exaltation of an Abyssal? I know their soul is destined for Oblivion, but is the spark a one-and-done usage for the Deathlords?</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Exaltations are as imperishable as Solar Exaltations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How much of their past lives do Abyssals typically remember? I've seen some stuff about the will of the Deathlords overriding things like personality to a degree, but not sure if that extends to the past lives. </div> </div> </div>Abyssals aren't substantially different than Solars in how they can experience and relate to their past lives. There may be some thematic and narrative differences, but it's not like Abyssals have a harder time accessing them than Solars.<br /> <br /> (Anything about the will of the Deathlords overriding an Abyssal's personality that may have previously been written will definitely not reappear in Ex3).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T14:24:52-07:00","id":1395911,"title":"","content":"Already starting to sound better than 2E Abyssals<br /> <br /> Now, fix Infernals too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T00:08:18-07:00","id":1395977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1395681-questions-on-the-nature-of-abysal-exaltation?p=1395866#post1395866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssal Exaltations are as imperishable as Solar Exaltations.<br /> <br /> <br /> Abyssals aren't substantially different than Solars in how they can experience and relate to their past lives. There may be some thematic and narrative differences, but it's not like Abyssals have a harder time accessing them than Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to know. I was after plot ideas about an ex-member of a circle that is now an Abyssal, that the Circle are ambivalent towards. The history that's been build up indicate that this Abyssal has died before as an Abyssal, and I want assure if that meant going straight to Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Now I just need 